From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: identity default domain for the SM8350 MDSS

The bootloader leaves the display running when it hands over: on the ROG
Phone 5 the MDP keeps fetching the splash buffer at 0xe5000000 (IOVA ==
PA) through the ASUS 5.4 wrapper and the kexec. qcom_smmu_cfg_probe()
keeps those boot streams in bypass, but as soon as the MDSS is added to its
IOMMU group (0.063 s) it gets an empty DMA domain and every MDP fetch takes
a translation fault (SIDs 0x820/0xc20, iova 0xe504d700...). The picture on
the command mode panel is lost ~0.06 s into the kernel, 25 s before msm
probes and ~30 s before the first frame.

Other Qualcomm MDSS compatibles already get an identity default domain for
this reason; add SM8350. msm still attaches its own paging domain when it
binds, so only the window before msm probes changes.

--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c	2026-09-29 20:58:52.698157526 +0200
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c	2026-09-29 20:59:01.900382601 +0200
@@ -425,6 +425,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8350-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-mdss" },
 	{ }
 };
